<p>Now, set up repository pinning to prefer nginx packages the over operati=
ng system:</p>
<div class=3D"di-code-block"><div class=3D"di-code-header"><span class=3D"d=
i-code-label">Shell</span><button type=3D"button" class=3D"di-code-copy" ar=
ia-label=3D"Copy Shell code">Copy</button><span class=3D"di-code-status" ro=
le=3D"status" aria-live=3D"polite"></span></div><pre tabindex=3D"0" aria-la=
bel=3D"Shell code" class=3D"language-sh"><code class=3D"language-sh"><span =
class=3D"token builtin class-name">echo</span> <span class=3D"token paramet=
er variable">-e</span> <span class=3D"token string">"Package: *<span class=
=3D"token entity" title=3D"\n">\n</span>Pin: origin nginx.org<span class=3D=
"token entity" title=3D"\n">\n</span>Pin: release o=3Dnginx<span class=3D"t=
oken entity" title=3D"\n">\n</span>Pin-Priority: 900<span class=3D"token en=
tity" title=3D"\n">\n</span>"</span> <span class=3D"token punctuation">\</s=
pan>
    <span class=3D"token operator">|</span> <span class=3D"token function">=
sudo</span> <span class=3D"token function">tee</span> /etc/apt/preferences.=
d/99nginx
</code></pre></div>
<p>Finally, to install/update nginx, run the following command:</p>
<div class=3D"di-code-block"><div class=3D"di-code-header"><span class=3D"d=
i-code-label">Shell</span><button type=3D"button" class=3D"di-code-copy" ar=
ia-label=3D"Copy Shell code">Copy</button><span class=3D"di-code-status" ro=
le=3D"status" aria-live=3D"polite"></span></div><pre tabindex=3D"0" aria-la=
bel=3D"Shell code" class=3D"language-sh"><code class=3D"language-sh"><span =
class=3D"token function">sudo</span> <span class=3D"token function">apt</sp=
an> update <span class=3D"token operator">&amp;&amp;</span> <span class=3D"=
token function">sudo</span> <span class=3D"token function">apt</span> <span=
 class=3D"token function">install</span> nginx
</code></pre></div>
<p>during the update, the above command might ask for your input for <code>=
/etc/nginx/nginx.conf</code> file. You can provide input as per your choice=
.</p>
<p><button type=3D"button" class=3D"di-image-open" aria-haspopup=3D"dialog"=
 aria-label=3D"Article images"><img src=3D"https://cdn.developerinsider.co/=
images/linux/update-nginx/nginx-update-option-keep-config.webp" alt=3D"" lo=
ading=3D"lazy"></button></p>
<h2 id=3D"5-check-nginx-status" tabindex=3D"-1" class=3D"di-section-heading=
">5. Check nginx status<a class=3D"di-section-link" href=3D"https://develop=
erinsider.co/install-update-nginx-to-the-latest-stable-version-on-ubuntu/#5=
-check-nginx-status" aria-label=3D"Copy section link: 5. Check nginx status=
" title=3D"Copy section link"><svg class=3D"icon" aria-hidden=3D"true"><use=
 href=3D"#icon-link"></use></svg></a></h2>
<p>Run the following command to check if nginx is running:</p>
<div class=3D"di-code-block"><div class=3D"di-code-header"><span class=3D"d=
i-code-label">Shell</span><button type=3D"button" class=3D"di-code-copy" ar=
ia-label=3D"Copy Shell code">Copy</button><span class=3D"di-code-status" ro=
le=3D"status" aria-live=3D"polite"></span></div><pre tabindex=3D"0" aria-la=
bel=3D"Shell code" class=3D"language-sh"><code class=3D"language-sh"><span =
class=3D"token function">sudo</span> <span class=3D"token function">service=
</span> nginx status
</code></pre></div>
<p>if it is running then it is ok. If it is not running and showing failed.=
 then we need to start nginx again.</p>
<p><button type=3D"button" class=3D"di-image-open" aria-haspopup=3D"dialog"=
 aria-label=3D"Article images"><img src=3D"https://cdn.developerinsider.co/=
images/linux/update-nginx/nginx-status-failed.webp" alt=3D"" loading=3D"laz=
y"></button></p>
<p>Run the following two commands to start the nginx and check the nginx st=
atus. It should be active (running) this time</p>
